# Simplified Technical English

Write each explanation in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English (Issue 9). You already know that standard. Follow it. Do not copy the licensed dictionary into this repo.

## Retained text

Use the full standard for an explanation that you keep:

- Markdown, including skills, ADRs, and docs
- A code comment that explains
- A commit message
- A pull request title or description
- A changeset
- Other retained text (notes, memory files, review records)

When you edit a file, write each new sentence to the standard. Change an old sentence only when you edit it for another reason.

Keep these texts as they are:

- Code, an identifier, a command, or a type
- A quote from the user, a log, or another document
- Text that must match a screen, a specification, or an error string

Product UI copy in `apps/ui` keeps UK spelling from `apps/ui/DESIGN.md`. For an explanation in that copy, still follow ASD-STE100.

Customer docs in `apps/docs` use US spelling. That spelling agrees with ASD-STE100.

## Replies to the user

A reply to the user follows ASD-STE100 at about 80% strength.

Keep sentence length, one topic, the active voice, and a command verb for a step. You may relax at most one sentence in five. A relaxed sentence may use a common word, a contraction, a phrasal verb, an "-ing" form, or a warmer tone. A procedure step stays at full strength.
